### The parent describes a sudden or worsening difficult phase around age two or three.

15 of 189 posts.

Parents describe an apparent switch around a second or third birthday, or a new surge later in those years: a previously easier child now screams, refuses, hits or reacts intensely to small frustrations. Many ask whether this is normal, how long it lasts and whether they caused it, even when they believe the behaviour is developmentally expected. Contexts mentioned include potty training, disrupted naps, a new puppy and starting preschool; the share does not establish which caused the change.

