### The parent wants a usable script or system for responding to difficult behaviour.

18 of 189 posts.

Parents of children aged two to almost four want exact language, age-appropriate consequences, or a repeatable system rather than a general parenting label. They question ignoring versus comforting, whether warnings are threats, whether discipline can yet make sense, and whether a consequence teaches the intended lesson; some share methods they say helped. Two accounts promote the writer's own developing resource—stories with guidance offered through DMs, and a printable kit—so their claimed benefits are resource-promoting testimony rather than independent reviews.

- "I am looking for online video-type parenting courses to teach me to better handle these moments as her parent, so I can teach her lifelong communication, emotional regulation skills, and behaviors for her to replace the defiant behavior and tantrums with. Looking for something that teaches exactly what to say or do (like, almost scripts), not just general concepts." [ar062-0045]
