Parents of two- and three-year-olds are responding to reports of hitting, pushing, biting, screaming or not following directions at daycare or preschool. Some describe actual expulsion, a threat of expulsion or repeated placement changes, while others worry about a first phone call or behaviour learnt from peers. They try books, rewards, roleplay, consequences and coordination with teachers, but say it is hard to intervene at home when the behaviour happens only at school. Explanations raised by parents or staff include language frustration, sleep, impulse control, teacher changes and a growing group; these remain their explanations.

