### The parent connects screen use with worse behaviour and struggles to limit or remove it.

3 of 190 posts.

These three accounts concern a two-year-old demanding particular TV content, a three-year-old's reaction to losing an iPad, and a family restricting weekday TV. Parents describe rising requests and tantrums, exhaustion after another baby, approved content and limits that did not settle the problem. One reports improvement after cutting back, another struggles through worse behaviour during removal, and one reports a spouse who opposes reducing TV.

- "first thing in the morning when he comes into our room, he finds our TV remote and hands it to me after waking me up. points at the TV and says tv?. I say no and he screams and cries." [ar051-0002]
- "My husband really disagrees with cutting screen time. It's like the only way he can calm our son down." [ar051-0008]
