**But:** nothing found against it.

## Across the on-niche posts

### The parent has already tried ways to change behaviour.

336 of 379 posts.

Attempts range from calm choices and routines to timeouts, restraint and spanking; trying does not establish success.

- "I believe in time outs, putting them in the corner, taking toys, having talks about why certain behavior is wrong, and yes, even spankings. None of it seems to matter with her." [ar071-0029]
- "At home, we are trying to provide predictable routines using a visual picture schedule." [ar025-0092]

**But:** Some report a useful adjustment. "Today I finally realised I needed to remind her that she was going to see it and that if she wanted to she could close her eyes.  So we “closed our eyes together” and I took her pajama pants off and viola no meltdown." [ar013-0055]

### The parent hears conflicting responses from relatives, partners and professionals.

181 of 379 posts.

Others reassure, criticise, advise punishment or report disruption; they offer no single agreed approach.

- "My family keeps telling me we need to bite her back but I just cannot bring myself to do that." [ar003-0076]
- "Today while working I get a message from the teacher saying my daughters behavior is disruptive to the learning of her classmates and she can not teach when she has these meltdowns." [ar037-0063]

**But:** Some reassure. "Everything that I see and that my pediatrician has told me says this is just the normal two year old life." [ar054-0047]

### The parent reports spending on care, alternatives and ordinary purchases.

14 of 379 posts.

Purchases include childcare, gifts, safety equipment and incidental spending, not only behaviour remedies; tuition’s recipient is unspecified.

- "My 3 year old has started biting her nails and by that I mean she literally has like half of her nail bed left bc she bites the rest off." [ar057-0039]
- "[…] I've bought the books, added new trains and little people to represent the little boy. We got the Yoto with Blippi. […]" [ar003-0096]

**But:** Payment need not deliver the hoped-for care. "we’re essentially paying a second mortgage for my daughter to get attacked." [ar082-0048]

### The parent names guilt, dread, anger or exhaustion alongside love.

268 of 379 posts.

Fear of injury and judgement, hurt, resentment and regret also appear.

- "I hate myself right now and I want to be a better momma, one that my boys deserve." [ar052-0005]
- "Part of me feels like I made a huge mistake having her, but the other half loves her endlessly and is so excited to raise her." [ar063-0049]

**But:** Hearing from others can bring relief. "[…] I can’t tell you how much of a relief it is to hear that it isn’t just me going through this. […]" [ar034-0110]

